{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And it shall give light.</b> Meaning, the menorah gave light toward the table that was opposite the face of the menorah, as it is written in the section ותכל: ״וישם המנורה באהל מועד נכח השלחן״ — by implication, the menorah was there to give light upon the table. And likewise it is written in the section בהעלתך: ״אל מול פני המנורה״ — that is, toward the table — ״יאירו שבעת הנרות.״ And the plain sense follows the one who says it was placed from east to west, for then it is possible that all the openings of the lamps faced toward the table. But according to the one who says it was placed from north to south, then one must say the central lamp faced west and the others faced toward the central one — it does not seem likely that it was made to give light upon the table. And you cannot interpret ״והאיר״ according to its plain sense as Rashi interpreted it."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:07.245312616Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}